                <pb facs="0278" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/92.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador White</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee instructs Mr. White to send the department a copy of the note from the
                    French Government accepting invitation to join the opium commission as outlined
                    in his telegram of July 10.)</p>
            </div>
